                            <a name="comment203"></a>
<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: Six Months of Famine
</h4>

<p>
Hey, Kruse.  I'm guessing you weren't old enough to vote for Clinton. Ever read a really old newspaper, say, circa 1960. There weren't too many f'n stories told in those grand old black and whites.  Maybe people are sick of spun, fluffy crap and just want stuff old school - a good read  driven by facts from face-to-face meetings - not tea leaves from reporters who work the phones and the Internet.  I think people don't read the paper anymore because a bunch of punkass young reporters working on the cheap are writing too much copy and are sucking the quality out of journalism. The Man is to blame, not you my son.
</p>
<div class="posted">Posted by:


		<a href="mailto:dave@dave.com">sommer</a>
	

 at November 10,2005 09:04
</div>
